From fb3af47c6ff47e968b404a185734a741b7065501 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:12:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(flowchart): one 11px arrowhead, cut under the head,
 straight into the side (Q1+M1, Q10)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Report §2.3. Every flowchart end glyph (arrowhead at either end, cross,
circle) is ARROW_MARKER_PX = 11 px in user space, so `==>` no longer draws
a ~22 px head and a linkStyle width shares the head (the `-u` marker
variants are gone; a coloured end is `<base>_<colour>`). Wider glyph
`M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z`. The labels, casing, router and layout room for a
head is that one size; quality::ARROW_LEN follows it. advance.rs draws the
same glyph via scene::arrow_marker_def and cuts its route the same way.

M1, painter-only (SceneEdge geometry untouched, hosts draw their own
heads): the SVG stroke stops ARROW_TRIM (half a head) short under an
arrowhead, refX putting the tip exactly on the border, so no butt end
shows beside the tip and nothing overshoots into the node. A single cubic
that still turns at a glyph end is painted with a straight head-long stub
along its end handle (the side's normal): head and the stroke entering it
point square in. One drawn-geometry builder (drawn_segs) serves the
painter, picking (edge_distance) and edge_end_tangent, so pick == render;
routing, ports and labels keep reasoning on the scene's cubic
(edge_polyline), so no route changes for how a head is drawn. Long
(dummy-chain) edges get a straight stub in their waypoints after the ports
and nudge settle the ends (edgepass::glyph_stubs), so hosts draw it too.
Class/ER graphs set Graph::edge_paint_width so their edges carry
paint_width from the first stage: no stubs or trims there (class.svg and
er.svg byte-identical).

Q10: EDGE_WIDTH 2.0, thick 3.5, node strokes 1.8 (hard-coded lid, bars
and final-state ring included), SVG padding 16 (SVG_MARGIN). The scene
keeps its 28 px MARGIN: shifting every laid-out coordinate flipped the
router's float-exact tie-breaks in the dense fixtures, a layout change
Q10 rules out; titles fit against the SVG's canvas edge.

Twin choice-fan labels whose rows are crossed by the twin's steeper line
may step beside their line anywhere along its far half (stack_fans), so
they keep FAN_SIBLING_GAP (choice_twin_labels... test).

Quality: end_tilt judges the glyph heading as painted (frame ends either
way across the border); new end_kink column (stroke at the head's base).
The yardstick and the casing measure the painted strokes.

Not done (see summary): the router's end stub stays one clearance long;
lengthening it in the search to 2 heads + a corner moved routes in the
dense fixtures (+12..40% overlap/tight). Router paths' heads are square
(the cut lands in their straight run) but end_kink counts their base.

Corpus (25 fixtures' 14 flowcharts): heads >10 deg off square 33 -> 14
static (12 of them back-edge bows, B3), 25 -> 26 routed (12 bows; most of
the rest are ends the ports stage turned round a corner).

Tests changed (intended output changes):
- diagrams_without_link_style_render_exactly_as_before: 3.5 px thick
  stroke sharing #arrow, the new #arrow def bytes.
- edge_markers_draw_at_the_right_ends: unchanged and passing.
- link_style_* marker tests: arrow__ff3 (no -u), refX 5, 11 px, wider
  glyph; a width alone no longer adds a marker def.
- flowchart_edges_are_painted_by_edge_path_d and
  edge_picking_matches_the_painted_strokes_on_every_fixture: the SVG
  holds edge_path_d_painted (the cut stroke); picking covers the whole
  curve (the head inks the cut).
- end_tilt_reads_the_drawn_heading_against_the_side: + end_kink.
Gates revised (tests/quality.rs, each with its reason in a comment):
DEFECT_BASELINE end_tilt 24|19 -> 8|19, max 86.5|128.4 -> 86.3|127.6,
band 117/46446 -> 119/47754 routed, x_drawn 521 -> 523 routed,
idiom_spline 19 -> 27 static (slanted last legs reclassified), end_kink
19|39 new; CHANNEL_MAX overlap 2920|7620 -> 3240|8420, overlap_max
1290 -> 1370 routed, tight 9350|21900 -> 10090|22000, hug 3110 -> 3120;
EDGE_CHIP_MAX routed 2 -> 3; dense-td static defects 42 -> 43;
GAP_FLOORS dense-lr 9.6 -> 9.2, dense-td 12.1 -> 11.3 static: all from
measuring the painted straight stubs (converging ends run parallel into
a side instead of fanning in); routes unchanged.

